        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0732" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300 114 /01.3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-10-23">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>887. United States Steel Products Company, 30 Church Street, New York, urging
                    through London manager that Embassy make representations to British Government
                    with a view to having raised embargo on shipments of manganese ore from India to
                    United States. Manager states company dependent upon this source of <pb
                        facs="0733" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/> supply and if embargo not raised will
                    sustain great loss. Further that two steamers loaded with company’s ore are held
                    in Bombay whose speedy release is desired. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
